  "details": "With the confirmed shutdowns of Rec Room (June 1) and Horizon Worlds VR (June 15), thousands of creators are looking for a new home. VRChat has the opportunity to be that sanctuary, but only if it bridges the gap between \"Unity-only\" development and accessible, in-game creativity.\n\n1. Universal \"Maker Pen\" & In-Game UGC\n\nWe need a native, in-game creation tool accessible to all players (not just VRC+).\n\nDorm Room Persistence: Every user should have a default \"Home\" instance that is fully customizable in-VR. Changes made with building tools must save automatically via Udon Persistence.\n\nThe Maker Pen: A spawnable tool for 3D drawing, prop manipulation (Move/Rotate/Scale), and spawning basic primitive shapes.\n\nQuest Compatibility: These tools must be optimized for standalone headsets to ensure the largest portion of the community can create.\n\n2. In-Game Costume & Mannequin System\n\nWearable UGC: Introduce a \"Costume Mannequin\" prop where users can draw or \"paint\" directly onto an avatar frame.\n\nAttachment System: Allow these drawings to be \"saved\" as temporary avatar accessories that follow the user’s bone movements.\n\n3. Earnable Economy (The \"Labor for Loot\" System)\n\nVRChat needs a progression system that doesn't rely solely on real-world currency.\n\nStandard Credits: Introduce a non-premium currency earned through \"Daily Quests,\" world exploration, and community engagement.\n\nThe Earnable Shop: A tier of avatar items and home props that can be purchased with earned credits, allowing free-to-play users to have a sense of progression.\n\nRetention: An earnable economy gives users a reason to log in every day, fostering a more active and dedicated player base.\n\nConclusion\n\nVRChat is the last great bastion of social VR. By adding these features, you aren't just adding \"tools\" you are providing a way for millions of displaced creators to continue their work and find a permanent home in your universe. \n\nWho's with me?",
